# tally 2.1.8 S9 (#179), E §5 step 1: "the answer is its booking from then on, so one answered by a refusal stays
# refused". pay's amount is a hole at its booking (1 February); v2 (known 1 March) states it and refuses its when
# (1 / 0); v3 (known 1 April) makes the when true again: from v2's known the booking is refused (b2, b3, the field
# a3) and, as a refused A0, no later version re-measures it, so no adjustment is made (n3). Before v2 (b1) the hole
# stands. 2.1.7's refcore refused two adjustments and kept the booking a hole; the M2 engine keeps it a hole.
=== m.tally
model h94
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-30
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source card "invented"

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

input dday: date

input amt: money PLN

input div: int

place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..

place world: outside lives 2026-01-01..

move pay: transfers
  on dday
  when 1 / div > 0
  leg cash from world to konto amount amt


version v1
  cite card
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  dday = 2026-02-01 "c"
  div = 1 "c"
  opening[konto] = 10.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "c"

version v2
  cite card
  governs always
  known 2026-03-01
  amt = 100.00 PLN "c"
  replace div = 0 "c"

version v3
  cite card
  governs always
  known 2026-04-01
  replace div = 1 "c"

ask b2: bal(konto, 2026-02-15) as known 2026-03-15
ask b3: bal(konto, 2026-06-30)
ask b1: bal(konto, 2026-02-15) as known 2026-02-20
ask n3: count(a in adjustments over 2026)
ask a3: pay.cash.amount
=== expect
a3: refused: RUN-DIV division by zero
  cut 2026-06-30
b1: ?"amt: no value" (amt)
  unfulfilled: pay
  cut 2026-02-20
b2: refused: RUN-DIV division by zero
  cut 2026-03-15
b3: refused: RUN-DIV division by zero
  cut 2026-06-30
n3: 0
  cut 2026-06-30
